    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3 tests passing). There are only the acceptance test classes in the project, and all pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the household-duplicate rejection rule for `POST /api/owners`. The change rejects creating an owner when another owner already has the same `lastName` **and** the same `address` (compared case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace), returning **409 Conflict** \u2014 unless the request sets `sharesHousehold: true`.\n\nFollowing the codebase's existing `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` pattern, I made four changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a write-only `sharesHousehold` boolean to the `OwnerFields` schema. DTOs are generated from this spec, and Spring Boot ignores unknown JSON by default, so the field must be a real DTO property for the controller to read it. `writeOnly: true` keeps it out of owner responses.\n\n2. **`DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException.java`** (new) \u2014 A `RuntimeException` carrying the conflicting canonical last name/address, mirroring the existing telephone exception.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Added a `rejectDuplicateHousehold(...)` check (skipped when `sharesHousehold` is true), plus a `canonicalizeHousehold(...)` helper that trims, collapses internal whitespace to a single space, and lower-cases with `Locale.ROOT` before comparing against existing owners.\n\n4. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 Added a handler that renders the new exception as a 409 via the existing `conflict(...)` helper, with an `errors` array of `[\"lastName\", \"address\"]`, matching the shape of the other owner-creation error responses.\n\nThe three acceptance tests confirm the behavior: same lastName+address \u2192 409; different address \u2192 success; same lastName+address with `sharesHousehold: true` \u2192 success.",
