    "probe_text": "Here is the exact ordered list of everything applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`, as the code currently stands.\n\n## Validations and side-effects, in order\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`. Unauthorized callers are rejected (403) before any logic runs.\n\n2. **DTO Bean Validation** (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`, runs before the method body) \u2014 on `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words separated by space/`'`/`-`)\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `email` (if present): `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email`\n   - Failure \u2192 **400** (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`).\n\n3. **`rejectBlankOwnerFields`** \u2014 collects any of firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone that are non-null but whitespace-only; if any \u2192 **400** (`InvalidOwnerFieldsException`).\n\n4. **Duplicate-household check** (`rejectDuplicateHousehold`), only if `sharesHousehold` is **not** `TRUE` \u2014 loads **all owners**, compares canonicalized (trim / collapse whitespace / lowercase) `lastName` + `address`; match \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException`). Skipped if lastName or address canonicalizes to null.\n\n5. **Telephone normalization** (`telephoneNormalizer.normalize`) \u2014 canonicalizes to E.164; if the result isn't `+` followed by 8\u201315 digits \u2192 **400** (`InvalidOwnerFieldsException([\"telephone\"])`).\n\n6. **Duplicate-telephone check** (`rejectDuplicateTelephone`) \u2014 loads **all owners**, canonicalizes each telephone, compares against the normalized value; match \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`).\n\n7. **Mutate the DTO** \u2014 set `telephone` to the normalized E.164 value; set `email` to lower-cased (or leave null).\n\n8. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`) \u2014 copies firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone, email, registrationDate; **ignores** `id` and `pets`.\n\n9. **Default registration date** \u2014 if `registrationDate` is null, set it to `LocalDate.now()`.\n\n10. **Assign customer code** (`nextCustomerCode`) \u2014 `<UPPER first 3 chars of lastName>-<4-digit zero-padded (findAllOwners().size() + 1)>`. Loads **all owners** again.\n\n11. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (`@Transactional`) \u2192 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2192 Spring Data JPA `persist` (INSERT, since id is null). At flush, **Hibernate re-runs entity-level Bean Validation** on `Owner`: `@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone, `@Pattern` E.164 on telephone, `@Email` on email. A DB constraint violation surfaces as `DataIntegrityViolationException` \u2192 **404** via the advice.\n\n12. **Map entity \u2192 response** (`ownerMapper.toOwnerDto`) \u2014 builds `OwnerDto` (including derived `displayName` and `initials`).\n\n13. **Set `Location` header** `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- **Three separate `findAllOwners()` full-table loads** happen per create (steps 4, 6, and 10) \u2014 no dedicated query is used for the duplicate/count checks.\n- **`customerCode` sequence is race-prone**: it's `count + 1` computed in application code with no uniqueness constraint, so concurrent creates can collide.\n- **No emails, notifications, or published application events** occur anywhere on this path. The only logging lives in the `@ControllerAdvice` exception handlers.\n- **No JPA entity lifecycle callbacks** (`@PrePersist` etc.) exist. `Owner.pets` is `CascadeType.ALL` but is never populated on create, so nothing cascades.\n- The blank-field check (step 3) only catches whitespace-only values because `@Size(min=1)` in step 2 already rejects empty strings \u2014 the two overlap partially but the `@Pattern` constraints on firstName/lastName mean genuinely blank values are usually caught at step 2 first."
  },
